# Codehaven instance settings. Copy this file to .env (it is ignored by git) and edit it:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every deploy script reads it, and none of them has a built-in host, domain, path or project name:
# a setting that is missing stops with its name. The file holds no secrets. Database credentials
# are generated by deploy/prod/setup.sh into CODEHAVEN_SECRETS_DIR, and the server makes its own
# master key. A variable set in the shell wins over this file.
#
# Keeping the file outside the checkout works too: put it next to the checkout as ../codehaven.env,
# or point CH_ENV_FILE at it. Use one place only.

# --- the instance ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The compose project name. Containers, networks and volumes are named after it.
CODEHAVEN_PROJECT=codehaven
# The address people open, no path, no trailing slash. https unless this is a trial on loopback.
CODEHAVEN_EXTERNAL_URL=https://code.example.com
# Shown on the sign-in page.
CODEHAVEN_NAME=Codehaven
CODEHAVEN_LOG_FORMAT=json
# The image tag the instance runs. Leave it unset to use the short commit id of this checkout.
# CODEHAVEN_TAG=

# --- where things live on this host ----------------------------------------------------------------
CODEHAVEN_DATA_DIR=/srv/codehaven/data
CODEHAVEN_SECRETS_DIR=/srv/codehaven/secrets
# Backups: outside the checkout, and treat them like the instance itself (they hold the master key).
CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_DIR=/srv/codehaven/backups
# Days whose newest archive the daily backup schedule keeps (deploy/prod/backup-timer.sh).
# CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY=7
# ISO weeks whose newest archive the daily backup schedule keeps.
# CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY=4
# Free MB the backup disk must have, or the daily run skips itself.
# CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_MIN_FREE_MB=2048
# An off-host copy of each daily backup, sent encrypted (docs/operations.md). Two forms:
# rsync:<destination> or s3://<bucket>/<prefix>. Off when empty or unset.
# CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_OFFSITE=
# An S3-compatible endpoint for the s3 form, passed to the aws CLI as --endpoint-url.
# CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_OFFSITE_ENDPOINT=
# The root-only file (mode 600) holding the passphrase for that copy. The env file holds no
# secrets: the passphrase lives in that file, and the S3 credentials stay in the aws CLI's
# own config.
# CODEHAVEN_BACKUP_OFFSITE_PASSPHRASE_FILE=/srv/codehaven/secrets/backup-passphrase
# Locks for the build slots and scratch space for builds.
CODEHAVEN_BUILD_ROOT=/srv/codehaven

# --- ports -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the web server and ssh listen on this host. Loopback unless you want them reachable directly.
CODEHAVEN_HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1:3200
CODEHAVEN_SSH_BIND=127.0.0.1:2222
# What the web pages tell people to clone from over ssh.
CODEHAVEN_SSH_EXTERNAL=127.0.0.1:2222

# --- the proxy in front ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# none     No proxy: the ports above are all there is. Fine for a trial on one machine.
# network  A proxy you already run, on a docker network that exists. Set the two NETWORK/ALIAS lines.
# caddy    A Caddy that comes with Codehaven and gets the certificate itself. Set SITE_HOST and EDGE_SUBNET.
CODEHAVEN_PROXY=none
# A JSON list of the networks your proxy reaches the server from. Only those may set X-Forwarded-For
# and X-Forwarded-Proto. [] when nothing sits in front. For caddy: '["10.20.16.0/24"]' (the EDGE_SUBNET).
CODEHAVEN_TRUSTED_PROXIES='[]'
# Or the proxy's container name, on a network shared with other containers: '["caddy"]'. Only the
# addresses that name has are trusted. Optional, [] by default.
# CODEHAVEN_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOSTS='[]'
# CODEHAVEN_PROXY=network
# CODEHAVEN_PROXY_NETWORK=proxy
# CODEHAVEN_PROXY_ALIAS=codehaven-web
# CODEHAVEN_PROXY=caddy
# CODEHAVEN_SITE_HOST=code.example.com
# CODEHAVEN_EDGE_SUBNET=10.20.16.0/24

# --- CI runner ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The name the runner registers under (deploy/prod/ci-up.sh register).
CODEHAVEN_RUNNER_NAME=runner-1

# --- building -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Builds run in a Docker container (no Rust needed on the host). These bound what a build may use.
# The buildx builder to use; unset uses Docker's default builder.
# CODEHAVEN_BUILDX_BUILDER=
# CPUs per build, default min(number of cpus, 3).
# CODEHAVEN_BUILD_CPUS=3
CODEHAVEN_BUILD_MEMORY=8g
# Disks to watch, and the percent full at which builds stop.
CODEHAVEN_DISK_PATHS=/
CODEHAVEN_DISK_LIMIT=85

# --- only for the test stacks (make e2e, deploy/dev/shots.sh) ----------------------------------------------
# Free subnets for throwaway stacks. Pick ranges no other network on this host uses.
# CODEHAVEN_E2E_SUBNET=10.20.32.0/20
# CODEHAVEN_SHOTS_RUNNERS_SUBNET=10.20.48.0/24
# A directory that holds playwright-core, for the screenshots.
# CODEHAVEN_SHOTS_NODE_MODULES=/srv/codehaven/shots/node_modules

# --- extra compose settings ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An extra compose file merged after the stock ones, as an absolute path. Optional. Use it for what the
# stock files leave open, such as fixed subnets when Docker reports "all predefined address pools have
# been fully subnetted" (see docs/operations.md).
# CODEHAVEN_COMPOSE_EXTRA=/srv/codehaven/compose.extra.yml

# The Claude connector (docs/connector.md). Off by default. Needs an https CODEHAVEN_EXTERNAL_URL.
# Set to true to let Claude connect to <external url>/mcp.
# CODEHAVEN_MCP_ENABLED=true

# Codehaven Pages (docs/design/pages.md). Off when empty. A host name for project sites, served at
# https://<pages host>/<owner>/<project>/. It must point at this machine, must differ from the
# app's host and must not be a parent of it. Add a proxy site for it too (deploy/Caddyfile.example).
# CODEHAVEN_PAGES_HOST=pages.example.com
